# env
#
# Ignore every .env* by default and re-admit only the template. The previous
# list named three exact spellings, and real secrets arrived in files called
# `.env.env` and `.env (2)` — the shapes an editor's "Save As" and a browser's
# duplicate-download actually produce. A deny-list of filenames is the wrong
# side of the default for anything holding a credential.
.env*
!.env.example

